From 6756ca99328dcb32b692e31b8bf1fd10e5f489f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:58:36 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 14/15] queue: advertise and validate per-image codec VP pools
 on ABI 2

Rebuild the earlier multi-VP pool table on bf49a31b while retaining its
queued SRAM transport, per-VP picture ownership and tagged VP DONE events.
Publish an optional AVM2 record and reject codec/engine mismatches before
feeding a program. The existing scheduler already overlaps different VPs
and starts PP in submission order, so its current ownership rules stay.

Include the non-LSR v3-t2 image in both build matrices. Mark T6040's pool
as inferred. Test every image's codec/engine pairs, reverse VP completion,
per-engine notifications, outbox backpressure and ordered PP.
[dylan: one co-author trailer of the original message is not reproduced here]

